==English==

===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*ǵʰley-}}
From {{inh|en|enm|*gloom}}, {{m|enm|*glom}}, from {{inh|en|ang|glōm|t=gloaming, twilight, darkness}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*glōm}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*glōmaz|t=gleam, shimmer, sheen}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*ǵʰley-|t=to gleam, shimmer, glow}}. The English word is cognate with {{cog|no|glom|t=transparent membrane}}, {{cog|sco|gloam|t=twilight; faint light; dull gleam}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ɡluːm/|a=RP}}
* {{IPA|en|/ɡlum/|a=GA}}
* {{audio|en|En-us-gloom.ogg|a=GA}}
* {{rhymes|en|uːm|s=1}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|-|s}}

# [[darkness|Darkness]], [[dimness]], or [[obscurity]].
#: {{ux|en|the '''gloom''' of a forest, or of midnight}}
#* {{RQ:Falkner Moonfleet|year=1934|passage=Here was a surprise, and a sad one for me, for I perceived that I had slept away a day, and that the sun was setting for another night. And yet it mattered little, for night or daytime there was no light to help me in this horrible place; and though my eyes had grown accustomed to the '''gloom''', I could make out nothing to show me where to work.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2022 January 12|title=News in pictures: Repatriated '66s' return home|journal=RAIL|issue=948|page=20|text=On December 13, Maritime-liveried 66051 powers out of the early morning '''gloom''' with three repatriated Class 66s, on the 0809 Dollands Moor Sidings-Scunthorpe Redbourne Siding.}}
# A [[depressing]], [[despondent]], or [[melancholic]] [[atmosphere]].
#* {{RQ:Robert Browning Men and Women|volume=I|poem=Childe Roland|stanza=19|page=142|passage=A sudden little river crossed my path / As unexpected as a serpent comes. / No sluggish tide congenial to the '''glooms'''— / This, as it frothed by, might have been a bath / For the fiend's glowing hoof—to see the wrath / Of its black eddy bespate with flakes and spumes.}}
#* {{quote-song|en|year=1956|lyricist=Mae Boren Axton; Tommy Durden; Elvis Presley|title=w:Heartbreak Hotel|artist=w:Elvis Presley|passage=Although it's always crowded<br>You still can find some room<br>For broken-hearted lovers<br>To cry there in their '''gloom'''.}}
# Cloudiness or heaviness of mind; melancholy; aspect of sorrow; low spirits; dullness.
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1770|author=w:Edmund Burke|title=Thoughts on the Cause of the Present Discontents
|passage=A sullen '''gloom''' and furious disorder prevailed by fits.}}
# A [[dry]]ing [[oven]] used in [[gunpowder]] [[manufacture]].

